      "writtenOn": "2019-01-10T02:59:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The variable name implies it\u0027s set by the host :)\nIf we want to generalize save_alarm for other cases than host alarm restoration, we need to keep host_rtc_alarm_set to store the state. OTOH, \u0027host_wake_time should be renamed as something more generic, like rtc_alarm_wake_time.\n\nDo you think save_alarm will be useful in other cases?",
      "parentUuid": "87d4c341_e1f482cc",
      "revId": "eec509118d5472a51df974d784cebeac598ba3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
