    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd3f1e37_12d8d2a0",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/clock-f.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-10T03:23:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I mean is this:\n\nset_rtc_alarm(..., 1);\n \u003d\u003e host_wake_time is set\nset_rtc_alarm(..., 0);\n \u003d\u003e host_wake_time is still set set\n\n__rtc_alarm_irq triggers due to the no save alarm, and resets host_wake_time. Is that expected?\n\nMaybe it is, but the comment needs to be updated: (host_wake_time.ts.val) means that an alarm was _saved_, not necessarily that the host set the alarm that actually triggered.",
      "parentUuid": "e569188c_fcf9f207",
      "revId": "eec509118d5472a51df974d784cebeac598ba3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8542b181_6f53e836",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/clock-f.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-10T19:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see.\n\nThe main (in most cases, only) caller of set_rtc_alarm() is __idle.\nIn __idle, once EC is woken up from deep sleep mode by rtc alarm, we cleared the pending irq before re-enabling interrupt (which is what CL:1390947 tried to fix).\nSo rtc alarm irq never fires in this use case.\n\nHowever, if someone else calls set_rtc_alarm (e.g. console command rtc_alarm) when host alarm is set, then yes, the scenario you said can happen - we may wake up the host before the alarm deadline passes.\n \nI\u0027ll fix it in a later patch.",
      "parentUuid": "fd3f1e37_12d8d2a0",
      "revId": "eec509118d5472a51df974d784cebeac598ba3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9adafe60_88a9afde",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/clock-f.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-11T02:53:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking closer, if we want to fix the console command issue, we\u0027ll need to use is_host_wake_alarm_expired() and check if the alarm comes from the saved one and then restore_host_wake_alarm() after resetting rtc alarm.\n\nBut this will add some corner cases and complicate the problem we originally aim to solve, IMO.\n\nI prefer to make this a expected behavior:\nIf someone other than __idle overwrites rtc alarm, when alarm irq fires, we wake up AP and clear save_alarm.",
      "parentUuid": "8542b181_6f53e836",
      "revId": "eec509118d5472a51df974d784cebeac598ba3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
